/**
 * Test skeleton for Story 1.6: 数据库基础（Postgres + Redis + ClickHouse）
 *
 * AUTO-GENERATED by QA Test Design (Turing, 2026-05-11). Dev MUST keep every
 * static (Unit) scenario passing once the corresponding deliverable lands;
 * runtime / CI / E2E scenarios stay `test.skip` with a pointer to
 * `docs/dev/logs/1.6-dev-log.md` §Integration / §E2E.
 *
 * Static scenarios parse:
 *   - Terraform module HCL (`infra/terraform/modules/{rds-postgres,redis-tair,clickhouse}/{main,variables,outputs,versions}.tf`) via raw text + regex
 *   - envs/staging wiring (`infra/terraform/envs/staging/{main,variables,outputs}.tf`) via raw text + regex
 *   - Migration files (`migrations/postgres/{atlas.hcl,0001_baseline.sql}`, `migrations/clickhouse/001_baseline.{up,down}.sql`) via raw text + regex
 *   - Bash scripts (`scripts/db-migrate.sh`, `scripts/db-doctor.sh`, `scripts/db-doctor/probes/redis-ping.sh`) via raw text + regex + stat mode
 *   - SQL probes (`scripts/db-doctor/probes/{postgres,clickhouse}.sql`) via raw text
 *   - Helm chart (`infra/helm/db-doctor/{Chart.yaml,values.yaml,templates/*.yaml}`) via raw text + selective YAML parse
 *   - CI workflow (`.github/workflows/db-migrate-check.yml`) via YAML parse + raw text
 *   - Operator docs (`docs/architecture/database-bootstrap.md`, `docs/architecture/source-tree.md`, `README.md`) via raw text
 *   - Story body for traceability invariants
 *
 * Test Design: docs/qa/assessments/1.6-test-design-20260511.md
 */

